From a0de74213fb1a303200fd1040233cf2d06b6cf23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:04:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] snxxx: Stop the client thread when a forced FW download
 aborts

When the FW integrity or FW/MW version check fails after a forced FW
download, phNxpNciHal_force_fw_download() releases the client message
queue and returns NFCSTATUS_CMD_ABORTED, and phNxpNciHal_MinOpen() gives
up through phNxpNciHal_MinOpen_Clean(), which never stops the client
thread. phDal4Nfc_msgrelease() then wakes the thread with an empty
message while thread_running is still 1, and from there on it keeps
calling phDal4Nfc_msgrcv() on a queue id of 0.

Mark the thread stopped before releasing the queue, so the wakeup makes
it exit instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kye574qt5dotSwvkUkvhEe
---
 snxxx/halimpl/hal/phNxpNciHal.cc | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/snxxx/halimpl/hal/phNxpNciHal.cc b/snxxx/halimpl/hal/phNxpNciHal.cc
index 75c505b..bdf8d6e 100644
--- a/snxxx/halimpl/hal/phNxpNciHal.cc
+++ b/snxxx/halimpl/hal/phNxpNciHal.cc
@@ -493,6 +493,10 @@ static NFCSTATUS phNxpNciHal_force_fw_download(uint8_t seq_handler_offset,
     } else if (status == NFCSTATUS_FW_CHECK_INTEGRITY_FAILED ||
                (phNxpNciHal_fw_mw_ver_check() != NFCSTATUS_SUCCESS)) {
       intptr_t client_id = nxpncihal_ctrl.gDrvCfg.nClientId;
+      /* The caller gives up on this open without closing it, so stop the client
+       * thread here. phDal4Nfc_msgrelease() wakes it up, and it exits on
+       * thread_running instead of handling an empty message. */
+      phNxpNciHal_kill_client_thread(&nxpncihal_ctrl);
       nxpncihal_ctrl.gDrvCfg.nClientId = 0;
       phOsalNfc_Timer_Cleanup();
       phNxpTempMgr::GetInstance().Reset();
